"Edralos","id":32432267,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNDMyMjY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32432267?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos","html_url":"https://github.com/Edralos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Edralos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T14:51:26Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T15:02:05Z","body":"Okay I think I pinpointed the origin of the problem. I don't know why but I unknowingly corrected my program while redacting the issue (I'm sorry for this 🥲 ). `WrappedCoord3D` initially looked like so :\n```cs\n[Export]\n    public Vector3 WrappedCoord3D \n    { \n        get => (Vector3)_child?.Get(\"Coord3D\") ; \n        set\n        {\n            if(_child == null)\n            {\n                GD.Print($\"buffering coord3D {value}\");\n                _temp3D = value;\n            }\n            else\n                _child?.Set(\"Coord3D\", value);\n        } \n    }\n```\n\nI had a hard time figuring this out because the issue wasn't appearing consistently between tries. It became consistent when I deleted the files in the `/.godot/exported` folder every time before exporting.\n\nSo what happened was that upon exporting, the console displayed an error about the getter being\nwrong, resulting in an export that nullifies values from the editor like descripted in this issue. However after correcting the getter by using `get => _child != null ? (Vector3)_child?.Get(\"Coord3D\") : new Vector3()  ; ` and doing an new export, the editor values are still nullified. The problem disappears only when I first delete the content of the `/.godot/exported` before exporting.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4344866877/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]